sx` now reads the field for the last 14 days and no longer looks up the format reset. The share note carries the new wording.\n- **Summed shares:** `expectedOptions` in `rcq.ts` adds up the shares of every label under one key at the chosen tier. A key with several labels is named by the key, so Azorius Control and Jeskai Control become one `Control` chip.\n- **Long tail:** `splitOptions` and `MAIN_SHARE = 0.02` are added. In `InputsCard.tsx`, chips under 2% sit behind an `Other (N)` button that toggles to `Fewer`. A picked chip stays visible even while the rest are hidden.\n\nOne deviation from SPEC.md: the spec shows the button only while some options are hidden. Mine also shows it while expanded, so `Fewer` stays available even if every hidden chip has been picked.", "ttft_ms": 1730, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 35444, "uuid": "25fbeabe-8d08-4360-b0de-7dd7d8606e06", "ttft_stream_ms": 1009, "time_to_request_ms": 53, "first_content_frame_ms": 1010, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
